  "exec_summary": "The European Union's Anti-Money Laundering Authority has published draft guidelines on ongoing monitoring under Article 26(5) of the Anti-Money Laundering Regulation, which will impact financial institutions' compliance obligations. In Belgium, financial services firms should take note of these developments as they navigate the EU's regulatory landscape. The guidelines aim to clarify expectations for ongoing monitoring, a critical component of anti-money laundering efforts. Meanwhile, the rejection of Dutch fintech Bunq's banking license application by a US regulator serves as a reminder of the importance of robust licensing and compliance frameworks in the fintech space.",
